IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `de-tanf`

-- Delaware TANF -- worked cases from the seat of the applicant or recipient. Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on
-- stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked against the Division's COLA notice or a case decision.
-- Expected results were worked by hand from the deposited text; where DSSM 4008.1.3 gives a worked example, the comment says
-- whether this encoding agrees with it (NOTES.md finding 2). Standards: DSSM 4007.2 as printed, family of 3: 185% $1,737;
-- standard of need $939; payment standard $338.

§ `Cases`

§§ `Families used below`

`three` MEANS `the DSSM 4007.2 standards for` 3

GIVEN `wages` IS A NUMBER
      `stage` IS A `Disregard stage`
GIVETH AN `Earner`
`an earner with` `wages` `in` `stage` MEANS `Earner` OF `wages`, `stage`, 0, 0, 0, 0

GIVEN `applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earners` IS A LIST OF `Earner`
      `unearned` IS A NUMBER
      `support` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `TANF family`
`a family of three` `applicant` `the earners` `unearned` `support` MEANS
    `TANF family` OF 3, `applicant`, `the earners`, `unearned`, `support`, 0, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

§§ `DSSM 4007.2 -- the standards`

#ASSERT `What are the TANF standards for my family` 3 EQUALS `TANF standards` OF 1737, 939, 338
#ASSERT `What are the TANF standards for my family` 1 EQUALS `TANF standards` OF 1024, 554, 201
-- Ten people: 8 plus 2 above eight: 3,516 + 710; 1,901 + 384; 681 + 138.
#ASSERT `What are the TANF standards for my family` 10 EQUALS `TANF standards` OF 4226, 2285, 819

§§ `DSSM 4004 -- earned income`

-- $400 in the $30 plus 1/3 months: 400 - 90 = 310; 30 + 1/3 of 280 (93.33...): 186.67 left (1/3 is not rounded here).
#ASSERT `the net earnings after all disregards of` (`an earner with` 400 `in` `in the four months of the $30 plus 1/3 disregard`) EQUALS 560 DIVIDED BY 3
-- $390: 300 after the $90; 30 + 90: 180.
#ASSERT `the net earnings after all disregards of` (`an earner with` 390 `in` `in the four months of the $30 plus 1/3 disregard`) EQUALS 180
-- $400 in the eight $30 months: 280. Past both: 310.
#ASSERT `the net earnings after all disregards of` (`an earner with` 400 `in` `in the eight months of the $30 disregard`) EQUALS 280
#ASSERT `the net earnings after all disregards of` (`an earner with` 400 `in` `past both disregards`) EQUALS 310
-- $80 earned: under the $90, nothing counts.
#ASSERT `the net earnings after all disregards of` (`an earner with` 80 `in` `in the four months of the $30 plus 1/3 disregard`) EQUALS 0
-- Dependent care: $500 paid for two children under two, capped at 2 x $200 = 400; $100 for one older child, under $175.
#ASSERT `the dependent care deduction for` (`Earner` OF 1000, `past both disregards`, 500, 2, 100, 1) EQUALS 500
-- The applicant test takes only the $90 and dependent care: $1,000 - 90 - 500 = 410.
#ASSERT `the applicant-test net earnings of` (`Earner` OF 1000, `past both disregards`, 500, 2, 100, 1) EQUALS 410

§§ `DSSM 4008.1.3 -- the worked examples`

-- Applicant Example #1: pension $150, earnings $400. Applicant net income 310 + 150 = 460, over the $338 payment standard:
-- denied. (The example prints "$460 < $338" but reaches the same result.)
#ASSERT NOT (`the family is eligible for TANF, on the tests encoded` (`a family of three` TRUE (LIST (`an earner with` 400 `in` `in the four months of the $30 plus 1/3 disregard`)) 150 0) `three`)
#ASSERT `the TANF grant for` (`a family of three` TRUE (LIST (`an earner with` 400 `in` `in the four months of the $30 plus 1/3 disregard`)) 150 0) `with standards` `three` EQUALS 0
-- Applicant Example #2: earnings $400, no other income. Applicant net 310, not over 338: passes. Grant: net 186.67, deficit
-- 752.33, half 376.17, capped at the payment standard: $338. (The example prints a deficit of $600 and a grant of $300, which
-- the steps do not produce: finding 2.)
#ASSERT `the TANF grant for` (`a family of three` TRUE (LIST (`an earner with` 400 `in` `in the four months of the $30 plus 1/3 disregard`)) 0 0) `with standards` `three` EQUALS 338
-- Recipient Example: pension $150, earnings $400. Net 186.67 + 150 = 336.67, under $939. Deficit 602.33; half: 1,807/6 =
-- $301.17. (The example prints $301: it rounds, the steps do not say to: finding 4.)
#ASSERT `the TANF grant for` (`a family of three` FALSE (LIST (`an earner with` 400 `in` `in the four months of the $30 plus 1/3 disregard`)) 150 0) `with standards` `three` EQUALS 1807 DIVIDED BY 6
-- The same with earnings $390: net 180 + 150 = 330; deficit 609; half $304.50.
#ASSERT `the TANF grant for` (`a family of three` FALSE (LIST (`an earner with` 390 `in` `in the four months of the $30 plus 1/3 disregard`)) 150 0) `with standards` `three` EQUALS 304.5

§§ `The grant`

-- No income: half of 939 is 469.50, capped at $338.
#ASSERT `the TANF grant for` (`a family of three` TRUE EMPTY 0 0) `with standards` `three` EQUALS 338
-- Recipient with $900 unearned: deficit 39, half $19.50 (not under $10).
#ASSERT `the TANF grant for` (`a family of three` FALSE EMPTY 900 0) `with standards` `three` EQUALS 19.5
-- Recipient with $925 unearned: deficit 14, half $7: "Grants are not issued in amounts less than $10.00".
#ASSERT `the TANF grant for` (`a family of three` FALSE EMPTY 925 0) `with standards` `three` EQUALS 0
-- Child support: an applicant with $150 support and nothing else counts $100 for eligibility (passes), and none in the grant:
-- $338.
#ASSERT `the TANF grant for` (`a family of three` TRUE EMPTY 0 150) `with standards` `three` EQUALS 338
-- A recipient with $800 unearned and $200 support: 800 + 150 = 950 over $939: denied. With $50 support: 800 passes; the
-- grant ignores support: deficit 139, $69.50.
#ASSERT `the TANF grant for` (`a family of three` FALSE EMPTY 800 200) `with standards` `three` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the TANF grant for` (`a family of three` FALSE EMPTY 800 50) `with standards` `three` EQUALS 69.5
-- With standards from a (hypothetical) current notice, 185% 2,000, need 1,100, payment 400: no income, half of 1,100 = 550,
-- capped at $400.
#ASSERT `the TANF grant for` (`a family of three` TRUE EMPTY 0 0) `with standards` (`TANF standards` OF 2000, 1100, 400) EQUALS 400

§§ `Eligibility`

-- Gross test: a recipient earning $1,800 past both disregards: $1,800 over $1,737.
#ASSERT NOT (`the family passes the gross income test` (`a family of three` FALSE (LIST (`an earner with` 1800 `in` `past both disregards`)) 0 0) `three`)
-- Exactly $1,737: not "exceeds" (finding 3).
#ASSERT `the family passes the gross income test` (`a family of three` FALSE (LIST (`an earner with` 1737 `in` `past both disregards`)) 0 0) `three`
-- Resources: $10,000 passes, $10,001 fails.
#ASSERT `the family is eligible for TANF, on the tests encoded` (`TANF family` OF 3, TRUE, EMPTY, 0, 0, 10000, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE) `three`
#ASSERT NOT (`the family is eligible for TANF, on the tests encoded` (`TANF family` OF 3, TRUE, EMPTY, 0, 0, 10001, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE) `three`)
-- s 503(a): a transfer of $500 or more without fair consideration, or an inmate: not granted. s 503(d): no nonsupport suit
-- or cooperation: not granted.
#ASSERT NOT (`the family is eligible for TANF, on the tests encoded` (`TANF family` OF 3, TRUE, EMPTY, 0, 0, 0, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE) `three`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the family is eligible for TANF, on the tests encoded` (`TANF family` OF 3, TRUE, EMPTY, 0, 0, 0, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE) `three`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the family is eligible for TANF, on the tests encoded` (`TANF family` OF 3, TRUE, EMPTY, 0, 0, 0, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) `three`)
-- The seat question, an applicant with $400 earnings, $50 care for one older child, $1,000 savings: passes (400 - 90 - 50 = 260).
#ASSERT `Does my family pass the TANF tests` 3 TRUE 400 `in the four months of the $30 plus 1/3 disregard` 0 0 50 1 0 0 1000 FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Its grant: 400 - 90 - 123.33 - 50 = 136.67; deficit 802.33; half 401.17, capped: $338.
#ASSERT `How much would our TANF grant be` 3 TRUE 400 `in the four months of the $30 plus 1/3 disregard` 0 0 50 1 0 0 1000 EQUALS 338

§§ `Appeal and reporting`

#ASSERT `Until when may I appeal to the Superior Court` (Date 1 5 2026) EQUALS Date 31 5 2026
#ASSERT `May I appeal to the Superior Court` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 31 5 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`May I appeal to the Superior Court` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 1 6 2026))
#ASSERT NOT (`May I appeal to the Superior Court` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 10 5 2026))
-- Appealed on day 20: fulfilled. Not appealed: no breach.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the s 520 right to appeal` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant or recipient` `appeal the hearing decision to the Superior Court` 20)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the s 520 right to appeal` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 40)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- s 510: reported: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the s 510 duty to report new property or income` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the recipient` `notify the Department of the property or income` 5)) EQUALS FULFILLED
